From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 18:16:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02640/11362] [outer-loop] Config Layer B tr87: scaffolding
 fixes reading (Tier 0) but rewrite-class needs a rewrite-specific digest

tr87 (hardest class, 2-D glyph rewrite) under the same generic scaffold: Tier 0 coherent -- NO
degeneration (move 1 made tr87 ramble a wrong rule; scaffolded it wrote clean code) -- but NOT grounded.
Concrete structural reason: tr87's editable region is 768 cells (16x48, 2-D) vs ka59's 38-cell 1-D strip.
The flat values=[...] digest of 768 cells is itself 768 numbers; the model spent its whole 1100-token
budget echoing that array as a comment and never reached a return (is_win returns None -> fires_on_win
False).

So the generic count/component digest does NOT transfer to the rewrite class -- not a reading failure
(reading is fixed), but a digest-shape mismatch: a 2-D glyph rewrite needs a per-glyph mapping digest
(grid of glyph cells + the reference-defined rewrite map), not a flat value dump.

Net across both targets: structured extraction fixes the reading bottleneck (Tier 0 on BOTH ka59 and
tr87, vs move 1 where both failed at reading); ka59 (count-class) grounds fully (Tier 2 relational);
tr87 (rewrite-class) needs a class-specific digest. Adversarial-verify clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
